# Route and limits

The route is one explicit construction. It first searches a finite grid in the supplied augmented Lie basis; a bounded traceless-logarithm existence argument proves grid coverage without selecting a computable eigenangle branch. It then realizes signed commutator trees with Taylor-jet error bounds, replaces every negative elementary flow by a finite simultaneous recurrence of both plant and actual-time blocks, smooths the resulting positive segments at unchanged total duration, and restores the physical identity phases and resource ledgers.

The main independent estimates are equations (10), (16), (18)-(22), (25)-(30) in DERIVATION.md. They are analytic, not test results. The auxiliary direct sum used in those equations is mathematical bookkeeping and adds no physical qubits or initialized ancillas. The recurrence search uses a fixed Frobenius-enclosure accuracy and a finite Q^(2d) candidate range, so no unsuccessful exact-threshold decision can stall it. The coefficient-grid search has the same strict-margin discipline.

For a certificate with maximum commutator leaf count ell, physical duration has the sufficient upper exponent ell+2d(ell+1), word count exponent ell, and inverse ramp-width exponent ell+1. The constants can be enormous and depend on the entire supplied certificate. There is no classical oracle-runtime bound, uniform shrinking-lambda/window result, polynomial qubit-size claim, prescribed completion time, physical actuator supplier or free memory reset.

No scientific computation was needed. No numerical fixture was predeclared or run. No metadata process failure had occurred before the two current metadata subprocesses; their actual outcomes, including any failure if one occurs, are recorded under metadata_runs. Earlier campaign failures are not rerun or recast as this theorem's evidence.

One pre-freeze drafting clarification made both finite certificate searches use a fixed upper-norm enclosure accuracy before moving to the next candidate, rather than leaving a reader to infer a terminating comparison near a threshold. A second made the endpoint trace-error allocation explicit. These were analytic wording/algorithm clarifications during drafting, not failed scientific runs. There is one current proof at the final recorded identity.
